     rrppcc..lloocckkdd [--dd _d_e_b_u_g___l_e_v_e_l] [--FF] [--gg _g_r_a_c_e _p_e_r_i_o_d] [--hh _b_i_n_d_i_p] [--pp _p_o_r_t]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rrppcc..lloocckkdd utility provides monitored and unmonitored file and record
     locking services in an NFSv3 environment.  To monitor the status of hosts
     requesting locks, the locking daemon typically operates in conjunction
     with rpc.statd(8).

     Options and operands available for rrppcc..lloocckkdd:

     --dd      The --dd option causes debugging information to be written to sys‐
             log, recording all RPC transactions to the daemon.  These mes‐
             sages are logged with level LOG_DEBUG and facility LOG_DAEMON.
             Specifying a _d_e_b_u_g___l_e_v_e_l of 1 results in the generation of one
             log line per protocol operation.  Higher debug levels can be
             specified, causing display of operation arguments and internal
             operations of the daemon.

     --FF      Run rrppcc..lloocckkdd in the foreground, rather than going into daemon
             mode.  This is useful if some other process uses fork(2) and
             exec(3) to run rrppcc..lloocckkdd, and wants to monitor when and how it
             exits.

     --gg      The --gg option allow to specify the _g_r_a_c_e _p_e_r_i_o_d, in seconds.
             During the grace period rrppcc..lloocckkdd only accepts requests from
             hosts which are reinitialising locks which existed before the
             server restart.  Default is 30 seconds.

     --hh _b_i_n_d_i_p
             Specify specific IP addresses to bind to.  This option may be
             specified multiple times.  If no --hh option is specified,
             rrppcc..lloocckkdd will bind to INADDR_ANY.  Note that when specifying IP
             addresses with --hh, rrppcc..lloocckkdd will automatically add 127.0.0.1 and
             if IPv6 is enabled, ::1 to the list.

     --pp      The --pp option allow to force the daemon to bind to the specified
             _p_o_r_t, for both AF_INET and AF_INET6 address families.

     Error conditions are logged to syslog, irrespective of the debug level,
     using log level LOG_ERR and facility LOG_DAEMON.

     The rrppcc..lloocckkdd utility must NOT be invoked by inetd(8) because the proto‐
     col assumes that the daemon will run from system start time.  Instead, it
     should be configured in rc.conf(5) to run at system startup.

